12. Append-only schema registry

Every schema that has ever written permanent data must remain available.

schemas.patala.org/
    core/
        event/
            1.0.0/
            1.1.0/
    atlas/
        work/
            1.0.0/
            2.0.0/
        assertion/
            1.0.0/
            1.1.0/

Every record stores:

{
  "schema_uri":
    "https://schemas.patala.org/atlas/assertion/1.1.0/schema.json"
}

JSON Schema explicitly recommends declaring the $schema dialect and a stable $id for a schema. This matters because JSON Schema drafts themselves have included breaking behavioral changes. 

Therefore each Pāṭala schema contains:

{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://schemas.patala.org/atlas/assertion/1.1.0/schema.json"
}

Never:

schema = "latest"

inside permanent data.

latest can exist as documentation redirect only.

