16. Enum evolution is more dangerous than it looks

Suppose:

rights:
    OPEN
    CLOSED

Then add:

UNKNOWN
FAIR_USE
COMPUTE_ONLY

Some client code will have:

if status == OPEN:
    ...
else:
    closed()

and silently misinterpret new cases.

So prefer:

controlled string vocabularies

plus:

UNKNOWN
OTHER

and require API clients to tolerate unknown values.

Do not make consumers assume the enum is permanently closed.

