43. Passages need stronger anchors than offsets

My previous:

TextSpan(start,end)

is insufficient.

Text offsets break when the text changes.

The W3C Web Annotation model explicitly notes that position selectors are brittle if the underlying resource changes, and provides complementary quote selectors containing exact text plus prefix/suffix context, as well as resource State information. 

Use multiple selectors.

TextAnchor {
    source_artifact_id
    selectors: [
        TextPositionSelector,
        TextQuoteSelector,
        XPathSelector?,
        XmlIdSelector?,
        IIIFSelector?
    ]
    source_digest
    normalization_profile?
}

For plain text:

{
  "position": {
    "start": 4811,
    "end": 4873
  },
  "quote": {
    "exact": "...",
    "prefix": "...",
    "suffix": "..."
  },
  "source_digest": "sha512:..."
}

Much more robust.

